<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador Jan-Jul coffee exports down 33.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Ecuador Jan-Jul coffee exports down 33.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuadorean coffee exports totaled 436,195 60-kilo sacks of coffee in the first seven months of the year, 33.5 percent less than in the same period of 1996, the National Coffee Exporters Association said Friday.</p>
<p>Coffee bean exports fell 47.5 percent during the period to 236,949 sacks. Exports of processed coffee fell 2.2 percent to 199,246 sacks.</p>
<p>Ecuadorean coffee producers are voluntarily reducing bean exports to try and push up prices.</p>
<p>((--Franz Bastidas, Quito Newsroom +5932 258429 e- mail: reuters1@reutersecu.com.ec))</p>
